    "body": "## What does this PR do?\n\nPrevent the Direct HF native adapter from silently discarding populated conversation fields. For example, a selected text `messages` prompt alongside structured `conversations` now reaches validation and is rejected. Two explicitly selected text columns named after chat fields remain valid.\n\nFixes NVBug 6900680.\n\n## Changelog\n\n- Preserve distinct source fields through native column renaming and reject populated destination collisions.\n- Reject ambiguous multi-column chat rows during shared SFT preprocessing; preserve overlapping-alias precedence and selected text-column priority.\n- Add real local-JSONL builder regressions and adapter coverage for conventional names, custom aliases, collisions, and null alternatives.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Regression/adapter tests against unchanged sources: 25 failed, 37 passed; candidate focused and adjacent tests: 139 passed.\n- Matched GPU validation: all 21 cases pass, with 15 valid controls trained for three optimizer steps and six malformed cases rejected. All 13 previously passing controls retain exact rows, token IDs, labels, masks, metadata, losses, gradient norms, and parameter updates. Recovered text-pair controls match the ordinary paired-text reference.\n- Tiny GPT training has finite logits, losses, gradients, and parameters, decreasing loss, and nonzero parameter updates. This covers actual Direct HF data feeding model optimization; distributed training and checkpoint/export are outside this check.\n- `uv run --no-sync pre-commit run --all-files` and `git diff --check` pass. Scoped strict mypy reports the same three pre-existing adapter typing errors before and after; no new errors.\n\n## Pre-checks\n\n- [x] Contributor guidelines followed; regression coverage added.\n- [x] No dependency or optional-import changes. No new user configuration to document.\n- [x] AI-assisted implementation and independent agent review.\n\nGitHub Actions CI is pending. Targets `main`; the mapped release label is not available.\n",
    "changed_files": 4,
